The decision tree executes cleanly, but the single `expectedPalindromeCounts` symbol makes the prover consider all 108 summary equations on each path. I’m removing that unnecessary indirection: `spec.k` will contain one disjoint reachability claim per palindrome interval, each with a constant tuple target. Together those claims are the same complete finite-domain theorem, and each proof path has at most seven comparisons.
